& [RegistryForm] is complete volatile custody
  + [CCS-001] CompactCoordinationRegistry is strict versioned JSON with registry identity generation ordered session records and registry digest
  + [CCS-002] CompactCoordinationRecord binds session identity sequence exact CoordinationToolContext current checkpoint or terminal outcome and record digest
  + [CCS-003] a record carries exactly one checkpoint or outcome
  + [CCS-004] registry and record digests are canonical SHA-256 over complete forms with only their own digest cleared
  + [CCS-005] validation rejects wrong profile map key identity digest sequence empty state or mixed state

& [HandleForm] is compact compare-and-set state
  + [CCS-006] CompactCoordinationHandle carries registry identity and digest session identity sequence record digest status optional checkpoint digest optional outcome digest and handle digest
  + [CCS-007] ready handles carry checkpoint only and terminal handles carry outcome only
  + [CCS-008] handle digest covers every field except itself

& [Commands] are closed
  + [CCS-009] OPEN requires expected registry digest unique session identity and context_json no larger than 4194304 bytes
  + [CCS-010] OPEN strictly parses CoordinationToolContext calls core BEGIN stores genesis and returns sequence one ready handle
  + [CCS-011] ADVANCE requires expected registry digest session identity expected sequence expected record digest and positive maximum_steps
  + [CCS-012] ADVANCE calls core ADVANCE and stores either one successor checkpoint or terminal outcome while incrementing registry generation and session sequence
  + [CCS-013] INSPECT requires exact registry digest and session identity and returns current handle without mutation
  + [CCS-014] READ requires exact registry digest and session identity and returns current handle plus exact compact record_json and record digest without mutation
  + [CCS-015] terminal sessions cannot advance and session identities cannot be reused

& [Transition] is pure before transport
  + [CCS-016] apply_compact_coordination_command accepts immutable registry and command and returns one successor registry plus typed response
  + [CCS-017] refused invalid and read-only commands return a byte-equal registry
  + [CCS-018] equal immutable registry and command values return byte-equal transitions
  + [CCS-019] no filesystem clock random provider model or external effect occurs in the transition

& [MCP] is one serialized volatile process
  + [CCS-020] cantor-compact-coordination-mcp exposes exactly continue_procedure_session over local STDIO
  + [CCS-021] one mutex serializes registry transitions so equal-head concurrent writes yield one success and one stale refusal
  + [CCS-022] MCP input and output schemas expand compact command response and handle forms but not CoordinationToolContext CoordinationCheckpoint or CoordinationOutcome
  + [CCS-023] ingress is bounded at 8388608 bytes and malformed oversized or unknown fields fail closed
  + [CCS-024] tool metadata is non-destructive non-idempotent non-read-only and closed-world
  + [CCS-025] restart creates a new empty registry and loses every session

& [Boundary] is a P0 local control plane
  + [CCS-026] no close deletion persistence recovery authentication authorization remote transport provider invocation prompt injection automatic selection effect or production deployment is included
  + [CCS-027] exact JSON strings are transport envelopes and only successful typed parse and core validation grant runtime use
  + [CCS-028] SHA-256 proves content binding not producer identity semantic truth or authorization

& [Acceptance] is finite
  + [CCS-A01] source SJS signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [CCS-A02] direct OPEN ADVANCE INSPECT READ terminal and replay tests match stateless core
  + [CCS-A03] stale duplicate zero-quota malformed oversized corrupt and concurrent equal-head cases fail closed
  + [CCS-A04] official RMCP subprocess lifecycle and compact schema and payload measurements pass
  + [CCS-A05] formatting warnings-denied lint workspace regression manifest audit narrative and scoped Git review pass

